{
  "info": {
    "name": "Parsi Post — Client Order API",
    "description": "# Parsi Post — Client Order API\n\nCustomer-facing ordering API used by the **ارسال با پارسی پست** WordPress plugin.\n\n**Base URL:** `https://post.pishgaman.top/api`\n\n## Authentication\n\nEvery request sends **two headers** (both required):\n\n| Header | Value | Missing → |\n|---|---|---|\n| `x-api-key` | your API key | HTTP 401 |\n| `office` | your Office GUID | HTTP 403 |\n\n> There is **no login / Bearer-token step**. The PDF/markdown vendor docs describe a `LOGIN` → `Authorization: Bearer …` flow, but the **live API rejects that** and uses the `x-api-key` + `office` header pair shown here (confirmed by live testing on 2026-05-24).\n\n## Response envelope\n\n`{ \"data\": {…}, \"success\": true|false, \"messages\": [ { \"persian_message\": \"…\" } ] }`\n\nOn error, read `messages[].persian_message` for a human-readable reason.\n\n## Setup\n\nFill the collection **Variables** (`apiKey`, `office`, and the UUIDs) once — every request references them. The UUIDs come from **Get Basic Info**. The values shipped here are the shared **test** contract; replace them with your own for production.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `weight` is in **grams**; locations are `\"lat,long\"` with no spaces.\n- **Save** creates a real, paid order — use with care.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Get Basic Info",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "office",
            "value": "{{office}}",
            "type": "text",
            "description": "Required. Office GUID (OfficeId). Without it the API returns 403."
          },
          {
            "key": "x-api-key",
            "value": "{{apiKey}}",
            "type": "text",
            "description": "Required. Your API key. Without it the API returns 401."
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/Ordering/ClientOrder/GetApiOrderBasicInfo",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "Ordering",
            "ClientOrder",
            "GetApiOrderBasicInfo"
          ]
        },
        "description": "**GET** `/Ordering/ClientOrder/GetApiOrderBasicInfo`\n\nReturns everything needed to build a price/order request for your contract: `provinces` (with their `cities` and city `id`s), `parcelTypes`, `insuranceTypes`, `boxTypes`, `paymentTypes`, and `extraServices`.\n\n**This is where you read the UUIDs** you paste into the WordPress plugin settings (service type, box type, parcel type, insurance type, payment type, sender city).\n\nResponse envelope: `{ data, success, messages }`."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
